<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Somali National Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1981–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SNM</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> National Movement was a rebel organisation founded in 1981, drawing mainly on the Isaaq clans of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, to fight the regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Siad Barre</a>. The government's bombardment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hargeisa">Hargeisa</a> in 1988 killed many civilians. After Barre's fall the movement declared the independence of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> in May 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/somali-national-movement.jpg" alt="Somali National Movement" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dabaqabad · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Somali_National_Movement.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
